th, td { border: 1px solid #9aa5b4; padding: 4pt 8pt; text-align: left; }
</style></head>
<body><h1>Capelli Sport — CS Certification Exam · Set 5</h1>
<p><strong>Name: ____________________   Date: __________   Score: ______ / 100</strong></p>
<p>Closed book. Answer in the voice of the agent handling the ticket. For each scenario, state <strong>how you handle it</strong> (route + action) and <strong>the one trap</strong> that would fail the ticket. <strong>Section A — 6 points each; Section B (multiple choice) — 2 points each. Total 100.</strong></p>
<hr>
<p><strong>Q1.</strong> <em>"I got two shipping emails with two tracking numbers for one order. Did you split my order? Is something wrong?"</em> How do you explain a mixed/two-shipment order?</p>
<p><strong>Q2.</strong> <em>"I understand there are delays, but I've heard nothing. Can you at least find out where my order actually is?"</em> How do you handle an ETA request when you don't yet have an answer?</p>
<p><strong>Q3.</strong> <em>"The jersey I received is completely blank — no logo, no design, just a plain shirt. I want the right one or my money back."</em> What do you do first?</p>
<p><strong>Q4.</strong> <em>"I ordered the youth size by mistake — I meant to get the men's. I'd like to swap it."</em> What is the correct handling?</p>
<p><strong>Q5.</strong> <em>"My son placed the order but our team credit didn't get applied. We want to cancel it."</em> Walk through the steps.</p>
<p><strong>Q6.</strong> <em>"I have no idea what size to order for my 9-year-old. Your sizing is confusing — which size should I pick?"</em> How do you help?</p>
<p><strong>Q7.</strong> <em>"I cannot get into my club's team store at all. Can you just give me access?"</em> How do you handle store access?</p>
<p><strong>Q8.</strong> <em>"You told me the item was out of stock last month. Is there any way to know when it's finally back so I can order it?"</em> How do you handle a restock request?</p>
<p><strong>Q9.</strong> <em>"If I don't get a resolution today, I'm contacting my lawyer. This is unacceptable."</em> How do you handle a legal/complaint escalation?</p>
<p><strong>Q10. Spot the mistake.</strong> A teammate drafted this reply — identify <strong>every</strong> thing wrong with it:</p>
<blockquote><em>"Sure! Your club store password is SOCA26. Also, good news — I can expedite your order so it ships overnight and gets there for your game. — Thanks!"</em></blockquote>
<p>List each error and give the corrected handling.</p>
<hr>
<h2>Section B — Multiple Choice (Q11–Q30)</h2>
<p>Choose the single best answer. 2 points each.</p>
<p><strong>11.</strong> A completely blank jersey (no logo/design) that arrives is handled as:</p>
<ul><li>A) A return</li><li>B) A wrong item — evidence photo, then the correct item</li><li>C) An exchange</li><li>D) No action</li></ul>
<p><strong>12.</strong> Two tracking numbers for one order means:</p>
<ul><li>A) A duplicate</li><li>B) A mixed/two-shipment order</li><li>C) An error to cancel</li><li>D) Fraud</li></ul>
<p><strong>13.</strong> When you don't yet have an ETA answer, you:</p>
<ul><li>A) Guess a date</li><li>B) Say you're checking with fulfillment and will update in 2–3 business days</li><li>C) Refund</li><li>D) Close it</li></ul>
<p><strong>14.</strong> Team credit wasn't applied and the customer wants to cancel. You:</p>
<ul><li>A) Refuse</li><li>B) Verify it isn't fulfilled, then cancel + refund</li><li>C) Reship</li><li>D) Escalate to the club</li></ul>
<p><strong>15.</strong> The correct size-help response is to:</p>
<ul><li>A) Direct the customer to the size chart (last gallery image)</li><li>B) Guess a size</li><li>C) Promise a fit</li><li>D) Offer an exchange</li></ul>
<p><strong>16.</strong> A legal-threat escalation should be handled by:</p>
<ul><li>A) Conceding immediately</li><li>B) Staying professional and escalating to a manager</li><li>C) Arguing</li><li>D) Closing it</li></ul>
<p><strong>17.</strong> A club password should be shared:</p>
<ul><li>A) After an ID check</li><li>B) By email only</li><li>C) Never — direct them to the club admin</li><li>D) For VIPs</li></ul>
<p><strong>18.</strong> A restock date given to customers should be:</p>
<ul><li>A) An exact date</li><li>B) No firm date; update once restocked</li><li>C) Within 24h</li><li>D) Next week</li></ul>
<p><strong>19.</strong> Approximate refund processing/appearance time:</p>
<ul><li>A) ~24h to process, 3–5 business days to appear</li><li>B) Instant</li><li>C) 30 days</li><li>D) 2 hours</li></ul>
<p><strong>20.</strong> Capelli misspelled the name on a personalized item. You:</p>
<ul><li>A) Say it's non-returnable and refuse</li><li>B) Treat it as our error — request a photo, then a same-size replacement</li><li>C) Offer an exchange</li><li>D) Refund shipping</li></ul>
<p><strong>21.</strong> To order for 2 players on one account you:</p>
<ul><li>A) Use two accounts</li><li>B) Place two separate orders</li><li>C) Use one cart: add player 1, proceed to cart, then add player 2</li><li>D) Call a manager</li></ul>
<p><strong>22.</strong> Which item is NOT returnable on its own?</p>
<ul><li>A) A mandatory-kit item</li><li>B) A stock jersey</li><li>C) Individually purchased socks</li><li>D) A hat</li></ul>
<p><strong>23.</strong> A customer says the site is "broken" on their phone. Likely fix:</p>
<ul><li>A) Use a different card</li><li>B) Turn the phone horizontal to see the CART button</li><li>C) Clear cookies</li><li>D) Call</li></ul>
<p><strong>24.</strong> A returned-to-sender package: you first:</p>
<ul><li>A) Refund</li><li>B) Confirm the address, then reship</li><li>C) Cancel</li><li>D) Escalate</li></ul>
<p><strong>25.</strong> "Enable Adding Individual Products" appears:</p>
<ul><li>A) At checkout</li><li>B) In the cart</li><li>C) At the bottom of the page after selecting the kit/player</li><li>D) In an email</li></ul>
<p><strong>26.</strong> A ticket awaiting customer photos is set to:</p>
<ul><li>A) Solved</li><li>B) Pending</li><li>C) Closed</li><li>D) Merged</li></ul>
<p><strong>27.</strong> A wrong size the customer ordered themselves is:</p>
<ul><li>A) Capelli's fault</li><li>B) A defect</li><li>C) Customer fault → return for refund</li><li>D) An exchange</li></ul>
<p><strong>28.</strong> Which internal name must NOT reach customers?</p>
<ul><li>A) UPS</li><li>B) Dan / BD / Operations</li><li>C) Capelli Sport</li><li>D) The club</li></ul>
<p><strong>29.</strong> Goodwill (a coupon/refund for trouble) is:</p>
<ul><li>A) Automatic</li><li>B) Never given</li><li>C) A manager-approved exception</li><li>D) The agent's choice</li></ul>
<p><strong>30.</strong> You must NOT promise a refund/replacement without:</p>
<ul><li>A) A manager present</li><li>B) The required check or evidence photo</li><li>C) The club's approval</li><li>D) A phone call</li></ul></body></html>